{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-classical-riemann-hypothesis","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Conjecture","doco:Section"],"label":"conj:classical-riemann-hypothesis","kind":"conjecture","title":"The Riemann hypothesis","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-riemann-zeta"],"tags":["tier:famous","riemann-hypothesis","millennium-problem","critical-line","zeta-zeros"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.ClassicalRiemannHypothesis","text":"classical-riemann-hypothesis.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"conj:classical-riemann-hypothesis\"></a><p>All non-trivial zeros of the Riemann zeta function <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\zeta(s)</code> satisfy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Re}(s) = \\frac{1}{2}</code>.</p>\n<p>In the language of the substrate, this asserts that the critical-line property established unconditionally at the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-scale persists through the classical limit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to 1</code>. The Hasse--Weil bound guarantees <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Re}(\\rho) = 1/2</code> for each local geometry individually. The Riemann hypothesis asserts that this alignment survives the adelic assembly into the global zeta function.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-riemann-hypothesis.md","heading":"Conjecture","number":"21.5.4","page":"b/conj-classical-riemann-hypothesis","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:BraidKnotOctonion.ClassicalRiemannHypothesis","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/BraidKnotOctonion/ClassicalRiemannHypothesis.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
